@@ -104,15 +104,29 @@ Each pet is recorded against exactly one owner, with a name, a birth date, and a
 
 A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`.
 
+<a id="req-vis-003"></a>
+
+A booking that was entered wrongly can be corrected afterwards. Both the date and the description of an already booked visit can be changed, and the correction is offered with the visit's current details already filled in `[REQ-VIS-003]`. A correction is judged by the same rules as a booking, so a corrected visit still carries a description and a date later than today. It replaces the visit it corrects: the pet ends up with the same visits as before, one of them changed. Nothing on the owner's record points to the correction yet, so it is reached only by asking for it directly `[REQ-VIS-003]`.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a pet, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then the visit is recorded and the booking is confirmed.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a blank description, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the description is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the date is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-002]` given a pet with earlier visits, when a new visit is being booked, then those earlier visits are shown with their dates and descriptions.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a booked visit, when its correction is opened, then that visit's current date and description are offered as the starting point.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a booked visit, when a description and a date later than today are submitted, then that visit carries the new details and the owner's record is shown.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a booked visit, when a correction succeeds, then the pet holds no visit it did not hold before.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a blank description, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused, the description is named, and the correction is offered again.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a date of today or earlier, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused, the date is named, and the correction is offered again.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given an owner's record, when it is opened, then it offers no way to reach a visit correction.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
+3. Correcting a visit that does not belong to the named pet is refused rather than changing another pet's visit.
+4. A refused correction leaves the stored visit exactly as it was.
+
+**ADR:** [ADR: Cancelling a Booked Visit Stays Out of Scope, Correcting One Does Not](adr/2026-09-17-non-goal-visit-cancellation.md)
 
